From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:29:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] flashinfer: port vllm#47979 uniform multi-token decode on
 Ampere

vLLM 0.30 gates spec-as-decode on a trtllm/XQA decode kernel, which is None
on sm_86. Without this patch MTP verify batches (q_len = K+1) take the
prefill path and FULL cudagraphs cannot capture them.

The FlashInfer native decode wrapper can plan a uniform q_len_per_req > 1
batch when the installed FlashInfer exposes `q_len_per_req` on
fast_decode_plan (0.6.18.post1 does). This patch ports part of vLLM PR
#47979 (an open draft upstream as of 2026-09-26) to 0.30.0:
  - allows spec-as-decode when trtllm decode is off and FlashInfer supports
    uniform multi-token decode;
  - reports UNIFORM_BATCH cudagraph support in that case;
  - keys the cudagraph decode wrappers by (batch_size, q_len_per_req),
    because q_len is part of the frozen graph shape (FlashInfer #3871);
  - plans the wrapper per request (num_decodes), not per token.

Needed on Ampere only. On Blackwell the upstream trtllm path already
covers this and the patch is inert.

Proof: FULL_AND_PIECEWISE capture completes with MTP K=3 and no
"not supported" cudagraph warnings.
---
 v1/attention/backends/flashinfer.py | 69 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

